    "text": "Let the position vectors of points &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&#39; and &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&#39; be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo></math> respectively. A point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> divides&nbsp;the line segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> internally in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is the origin and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>OB</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi>OP</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mover><mi>OA</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>OP</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
